1,Simeku language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/simeku_language,"The core vocabulary of Simeku, a South Bougainville language spoken in the mountainous regions of central Bougainville, reflects its genetic ties to the broader South Bougainville family while incorporating terms adapted to the local highland environment.",Simeku,South Bougainville
2,SOUTH CENTRAL BOUGAINVILLE (2025) - Wilson Pulu ... - YouTubeWilson Pulu x ABZ MON - South Central Bougainville (Official ...Simeku language explainedSaveLongGod | Bougainville (ARoB)S i me k u l an gu age,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GpHh3hP_iYg,"Feb 18, 2025 · Enjoy the videos and music you love, upload original content, and share it all with friends, family, and the world on YouTube. May 17, 2026 · This song blends modern beats with rich island melodies, celebrating the culture, resilience, and pride of Bougainville. Let the rhythm take you on a journey through the heart of the islands! Simeku is a South Bougainville language spoken in the mountains of southern Bougainville Province, Papua New Guinea. South Bougainville Bannoni - Banoni, Tsunari [bcm] Lawunuia - Nagarige, Nagarege, Naghareghe, Piva [tgi] Sibe - Sibbe, Sibe-Nagovisi, Nagovisi [nco] Siwai - Musa, Musan, Musian, Siafli, Siwai [siw] Terei - Buin, Telei, Rugara [buo] Uisai [uis] Uruava [urv] Jul 25, 2020 · Simeku language Simeku is an South Bougainville language spoken in the mountains of southern Bougainville Province, Papua New Guinea.",Simeku,South Bougainville
